ntral\" (located by the Coast & Geodetic Survey and described as follows:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372582; common-crawl capture 2025-09-12T17:26:28Z; unnumbered paragraph 8","sha256":"cd01b800e3ac77e24e0fea1b647ab870bdc0b282390e5b4d766bd5a7f46e58d3","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8480-excluding-certain-land-from-the-chugach-national-forest-and-reserving"},"scope_id":"EO:8480#p8","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Latitude 60°51'40.77\"; longitude 149°01\"25.10\"; Central is on the most easterly point on the north side of Turnagain Arm that can be seen from Kern Creek. It is just east of Mile 67 on the Alaska Northern Ry. The station mark is a metal plate set in cement at the surface of the ground on the highest part of the grassy elevation on the upper side of the railroad cut.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372582; common-crawl capture 2025-09-12T17:26:28Z; unnumbered paragraph 9","sha256":"cd01b800e3ac77e24e0fea1b647ab870bdc0b282390e5b4d766bd5a7f46e58d3","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-8480-excluding-certain-land-from-the-chugach-national-forest-and-reserving"},"scope_id":"EO:8480#p9","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Reference mark No. 1 is a nail in a blazed spruce back of the signal. No. 2 is a nail in a blazed spruce to the west.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"American Presidency Project web page (transcription; not an official edition); APP node 372582; common-crawl capture 2025-09-12T17:26:28Z; unnumbered paragraph 10","sha256":"cd01b800e3ac77e24e0fea1b647ab870bdc0b282390e5b4d766bd5a7f46e58d3","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/execu